# config: mock-slowscore.json
#
# A new game asked for while the game thread is scoring, or replaying a position
# into the engines, must be deferred like one asked for during a genmove
# (ADR-0001). runWhenEngineFree() decided "busy" from the player on move alone,
# and neither of those has one — so it ran the action inline, and the
# interrupt() inside it joined the game thread from the UI thread: the window
# frozen for as long as the engine took, up to the 30 s scoring timeout.
#
# `deferred_task true` straight after the command is the evidence: deferred
# means the UI thread came back at once; inline, it would be false, and late.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white human
wait_idle

# --- While scoring ----------------------------------------------------------
pass
wait_until move_count >= 1
pass
wait_until msg calculating_score
new_game 13
expect deferred_task true
wait_idle
expect board_size 13
expect move_count 0

# --- While the engines are being resynchronised -----------------------------
new_game 9
wait_until engine_sync syncing
new_game 13
expect deferred_task true
wait_idle
expect board_size 13
expect engine_sync synced
